    {
      "record_id": "switch:locres:set-02:ST_SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12:SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12_004:d82ff793",
      "source": {
        "set": "set-02",
        "namespace": "ST_SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12",
        "key": "SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12_004",
        "jp_record_id": "switch:locres:set-02:ST_SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12:SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12_004:d82ff793",
        "official_en_record_id": "switch:locres:set-02:ST_SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12:SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12_004:d82ff793",
        "jp_sha256": "51f7cbfd6dba646deefa5369b09f0122ef8419c1a1df6e4ca0bff6f72a6bd281",
        "official_en_sha256": "43e5a9683862acbaaf393e52ff71817c9424f2a35560a716142d6a03d2e576f1"
      },
      "text": {
        "jp": "だけど橋を渡らなければ、世界は広がらない。\r\n立ち止まるか、前に進むか、ふたつにひとつだ。",
        "official_en": "But without crossing, you cannot expand your horizons—both literally and figuratively. In the end, you face only two choices: stop in your tracks, or keep moving forward.",
        "real_en": "But if we never cross bridges, our world will never open up. We can either stand still or move forward."
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "CHANGE"
      },
      "function": "dialogue_line",
      "context": {
        "scene_ref": "ST_SubEv_C09_Gilgamesh_12",
